"""A1b: the seed channel must be DECLARED, MONOTONE and NULL AT ZERO.

After the trail rewrite, e is the SPEED label and the seed picks the trail DIRECTION.
The residual is therefore no longer a pixel-length with полуan e-proportional bound
(it is the area of a streak whose length is e*0.55*r_sub): what must hold is the order
structure that downstream training can read.

  A1b1  resid(e=0 sigma=0) == 0                 seed is null on a motionless scene
  A1b2  resid(e) non-decreasing in e            speed label is wired into pixels kam
  A1b3  resid(sigma) non-decreasing in sigma    noise adds variance, never hides NOD

The old pixel-bound form (resid <= 0.05*e*n) was calibrated against anchor jitter and is
retired: anchor jitter moved <= ose 0.05*r_sub of coverage, below one code step on flat
background, which is why it measured  Risk 0 for four of five ids.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import os
